WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.200 --> 00:00:03.520
- Our priority is to have Black, Brown,

00:00:03.520 --> 00:00:06.330
women-led businesses on our shelves.

00:00:06.330 --> 00:00:07.980
- There's just not enough, right?

00:00:09.610 --> 00:00:12.400
- People told me that this
industry was for White people.

00:00:12.400 --> 00:00:14.320
That as a Black person,

00:00:14.320 --> 00:00:17.680
that I was opening myself
up for being arrested.

00:00:17.680 --> 00:00:20.820
That I was never going to
be able to get investment.

00:00:20.820 --> 00:00:22.063
I was out pitching.

00:00:23.160 --> 00:00:25.033
I needed a lead investor.

00:00:25.950 --> 00:00:27.570
- [Narrator] Whitney
Beatty recently received

00:00:27.570 --> 00:00:30.050
an investment of just under
half a million dollars

00:00:30.050 --> 00:00:32.140
from a fund launched by Jay Z

00:00:32.140 --> 00:00:33.730
and a group of cannabis companies

00:00:33.730 --> 00:00:36.240
who together are called
The Parent Company.

00:00:36.240 --> 00:00:39.740
The fund will have an initial
investment of $10 million.

00:00:39.740 --> 00:00:42.230
- You've been pushing the boulder uphill

00:00:42.230 --> 00:00:44.000
for so long and finally,

00:00:44.000 --> 00:00:46.490
someone has come to push it with you.

00:00:46.490 --> 00:00:48.977
Not just someone, it's like Jay Z

00:00:48.977 --> 00:00:53.093
has come to push it with you
of all the people in the world.

00:00:54.360 --> 00:00:56.050
- [Narrator] In an interview
with The Wall Street Journal

00:00:56.050 --> 00:00:57.320
earlier this year,

00:00:57.320 --> 00:00:58.960
Jay Z said he was motivated

00:00:58.960 --> 00:01:01.493
by an imbalance in the marijuana industry.

00:01:02.330 --> 00:01:04.230
Statistics show that while Black people

00:01:04.230 --> 00:01:05.740
were nearly four times more likely

00:01:05.740 --> 00:01:08.760
than Whites to be arrested
for marijuana possession,

00:01:08.760 --> 00:01:11.550
they make up only a small
number of those profiting

00:01:11.550 --> 00:01:14.573
from the multi-billion dollar
legalized pot industry.

00:01:16.170 --> 00:01:18.540
- It's happening for a number of reasons,

00:01:18.540 --> 00:01:20.630
and a lot of them are financial.

00:01:20.630 --> 00:01:22.013
- [Woman] That'd be awesome.

00:01:23.409 --> 00:01:26.060
- It costs about 1.5 million, 2 million

00:01:26.060 --> 00:01:27.860
to open a dispensary in the LA area.

00:01:28.980 --> 00:01:32.150
I can't go to the SBA and ask for a loan.

00:01:32.150 --> 00:01:34.830
You can't go to Bank of America

00:01:34.830 --> 00:01:37.600
or Wells Fargo and ask for a business loan

00:01:37.600 --> 00:01:39.840
because this is still federally illegal.

00:01:39.840 --> 00:01:41.150
And you're stuck in a space

00:01:41.150 --> 00:01:44.150
where you need to raise money from VCs

00:01:44.150 --> 00:01:46.680
or from angel investors.

00:01:46.680 --> 00:01:49.480
People of color generally don't have a lot

00:01:49.480 --> 00:01:51.530
of angel investors within their networks.

00:01:52.474 --> 00:01:54.340
(hammer banging)

00:01:54.340 --> 00:01:55.610
- [Narrator] Beatty hopes investment

00:01:55.610 --> 00:01:58.160
from the Jay Z fund will
help her meet her goal

00:01:58.160 --> 00:01:59.260
of opening a dispensary

00:01:59.260 --> 00:02:02.410
in the highly competitive Los
Angeles market by September.

00:02:02.410 --> 00:02:05.600
- So they'll come in and
you'll have signage or a kiosk.

00:02:05.600 --> 00:02:07.780
My 401(k) does not exist.

00:02:07.780 --> 00:02:09.880
All in, the chips are here.

00:02:09.880 --> 00:02:11.660
If this doesn't happen,

00:02:11.660 --> 00:02:14.360
I don't even wanna
think about what happens

00:02:14.360 --> 00:02:15.450
if this doesn't happen.

00:02:15.450 --> 00:02:17.213
So are we still looking at.

00:02:18.659 --> 00:02:19.492
- Beginning of August?

00:02:19.492 --> 00:02:20.590
- Beginning of August?
- Yes.

00:02:21.733 --> 00:02:25.610
♪ And then a hero comes along ♪

00:02:25.610 --> 00:02:27.130
- [Narrator] States and municipalities

00:02:27.130 --> 00:02:29.410
have also tried to help
minority representation

00:02:29.410 --> 00:02:32.160
in the industry through
social equity programs

00:02:32.160 --> 00:02:35.103
that reserve cannabis
licenses for those groups.

00:02:36.330 --> 00:02:37.760
- If we're specifically talking

00:02:37.760 --> 00:02:40.740
about equity and licensing,

00:02:40.740 --> 00:02:44.060
then I would describe that program

00:02:44.060 --> 00:02:46.430
as an effort to reduce barriers

00:02:46.430 --> 00:02:50.110
to entering the legal cannabis
market for communities

00:02:50.110 --> 00:02:53.620
who have been historically
criminalized by cannabis.

00:02:53.620 --> 00:02:55.410
- [Narrator] Cat Packer oversees LA's

00:02:55.410 --> 00:02:57.770
cannabis regulations and licensing.

00:02:57.770 --> 00:02:59.990
- A lot of the feedback
today that we received

00:02:59.990 --> 00:03:03.340
is just that the process takes too long,

00:03:03.340 --> 00:03:07.110
and that the delays are extremely costly

00:03:07.110 --> 00:03:08.940
to social equity applicants.

00:03:08.940 --> 00:03:11.000
- This is the first
time I've seen a T-shirt

00:03:11.000 --> 00:03:12.263
with JV on it.

00:03:13.470 --> 00:03:15.970
- [Narrator] Beatty was
one of those applicants.

00:03:15.970 --> 00:03:20.050
She first applied for her
dispensary license in 2019.

00:03:20.050 --> 00:03:21.520
Soon after qualifying,

00:03:21.520 --> 00:03:23.570
she struck a deal with
a venture capital firm.

00:03:23.570 --> 00:03:25.500
- I went in for a meeting in February

00:03:25.500 --> 00:03:28.380
and I asked them about
their cash viability,

00:03:28.380 --> 00:03:30.150
and they said, "We have the money."

00:03:30.150 --> 00:03:33.013
And two weeks later they
said, "We're closing.

00:03:34.090 --> 00:03:35.597
And it's over."

00:03:37.530 --> 00:03:40.070
The legal cannabis
industry was much different

00:03:40.070 --> 00:03:42.110
when Wanda James and her husband opened

00:03:42.110 --> 00:03:44.283
their first dispensary in Colorado.

00:03:45.140 --> 00:03:47.340
- We opened up our dispensary in 2009.

00:03:47.340 --> 00:03:49.190
There were no social equity programs.

00:03:50.780 --> 00:03:53.140
The cost to open up a dispensary

00:03:53.140 --> 00:03:54.610
was the cost of your lease.

00:03:54.610 --> 00:03:56.300
So our first dispensary,

00:03:56.300 --> 00:03:58.130
including our grow facility,

00:03:58.130 --> 00:04:01.143
probably cost us in the
ballpark of about $200,000.

00:04:02.630 --> 00:04:05.210
We wanted to be able to use the dispensary

00:04:05.210 --> 00:04:08.023
to talk about mass incarceration.

00:04:09.750 --> 00:04:12.193
My brother's crime was
four ounces of weed.

00:04:13.140 --> 00:04:15.300
And that four ounces of
weed cost him 10 years

00:04:15.300 --> 00:04:17.493
of his life in the legal system.

00:04:19.360 --> 00:04:21.100
- [Narrator] James has
worked as a consultant,

00:04:21.100 --> 00:04:23.390
helping several states and municipalities

00:04:23.390 --> 00:04:25.840
create cannabis social equity policies.

00:04:25.840 --> 00:04:27.440
- If you're one of the
very fortunate people

00:04:27.440 --> 00:04:28.910
to be able to get a license,

00:04:28.910 --> 00:04:32.320
hopefully, the social
equity program allows

00:04:32.320 --> 00:04:35.250
for some type of funding from the state.

00:04:35.250 --> 00:04:40.250
- The reality is is that while
we are disbursing $6 million

00:04:40.960 --> 00:04:43.930
among potentially hundreds
of different applicants,

00:04:43.930 --> 00:04:45.880
our applicants are gonna be competing

00:04:45.880 --> 00:04:50.110
with businesses who alone have
multimillion dollar budget.

00:04:50.110 --> 00:04:51.680
- The issue that we see right now

00:04:51.680 --> 00:04:54.260
with social equity
across the United States

00:04:54.260 --> 00:04:57.588
is we have yet to see any
social equity program work.

00:04:57.588 --> 00:05:00.430
(pensive music)

00:05:00.430 --> 00:05:03.130
- [Narrator] That's where
funds like Jay Z's come in.

00:05:03.130 --> 00:05:06.910
Data shows that between 2013 to 2017,

00:05:06.910 --> 00:05:09.180
only 1% of US startup founders

00:05:09.180 --> 00:05:12.273
that received venture capital were Black.

00:05:12.273 --> 00:05:15.322
(sander buzzing)
(hammer banging)

00:05:15.322 --> 00:05:16.155
(boards falling)

00:05:16.155 --> 00:05:17.120
The money Beatty received

00:05:17.120 --> 00:05:18.883
has kept her on track so far.

00:05:19.811 --> 00:05:21.156
- You've got gorgeous hidden lights.

00:05:21.156 --> 00:05:22.040
- Isn't it beautiful?

00:05:22.040 --> 00:05:24.670
- [Narrator] But she still
needs to finish construction,

00:05:24.670 --> 00:05:26.840
and purchase inventory, like edibles

00:05:26.840 --> 00:05:28.749
from LA's Madame Munchie.

00:05:28.749 --> 00:05:30.244
- This kitchen.

00:05:30.244 --> 00:05:31.893
- It smells so good.
- It smells so good.

00:05:31.893 --> 00:05:34.458
- What are your mins?
What are your minimums?

00:05:34.458 --> 00:05:37.526
- We don't really have them
with this distro company.

00:05:37.526 --> 00:05:39.550
Especially since you're here in LA,

00:05:39.550 --> 00:05:41.019
I don't think we'll have a problem

00:05:41.019 --> 00:05:43.769
with whatever order size
you're gonna wanna start with.

00:05:45.193 --> 00:05:48.120
(boards falling)
(hammer banging)

00:05:48.120 --> 00:05:50.620
- We've got full-out
demolition going right now.

00:05:50.620 --> 00:05:54.630
We are in the middle of a
full build of our space.

00:05:54.630 --> 00:05:57.430
That has been covered
completely by this part

00:05:57.430 --> 00:05:58.890
of the investment.

00:05:58.890 --> 00:06:03.293
We are moving forward on all
cylinders because of this.

00:06:04.550 --> 00:06:06.810
- Any time there is money
out there to be had,

00:06:06.810 --> 00:06:09.410
I encourage all entrepreneurs

00:06:09.410 --> 00:06:12.060
to always go after every
dollar that's out there.

00:06:12.060 --> 00:06:14.840
But let's be real of what
the real effectiveness

00:06:14.840 --> 00:06:16.103
of those funds are.

00:06:17.720 --> 00:06:20.910
- [Narrator] Beatty needs
to raise over $300,000 more.

00:06:20.910 --> 00:06:22.270
It's unclear whether she'll be able

00:06:22.270 --> 00:06:24.370
to open her doors to start sales

00:06:24.370 --> 00:06:26.483
by her projected September launch date.

00:06:27.980 --> 00:06:30.211
- My bottom line comes down to the cash.

00:06:30.211 --> 00:06:32.470
There's never enough money.

00:06:32.470 --> 00:06:33.660
There's never enough money.

00:06:33.660 --> 00:06:35.290
I have been waiting for my license

00:06:35.290 --> 00:06:37.493
since September 3rd, 2019.

00:06:38.620 --> 00:06:43.420
I've been losing money for 22 months now.

00:06:43.420 --> 00:06:44.850
- We have a 10-head embroidery team

00:06:44.850 --> 00:06:47.000
of which we just did the hats.

00:06:47.000 --> 00:06:48.790
- There's no room for failure here.

00:06:48.790 --> 00:06:50.300
There really isn't.

00:06:50.300 --> 00:06:52.810
We are eight weeks from greatness

00:06:52.810 --> 00:06:54.409
or eight weeks from disaster.

00:06:54.409 --> 00:06:59.409
(dramatic music)
(gate squeaking)

